\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Mayor Lesser provided remarks honoring Bob White, a cherished longtime Manhattan Beach resident whose decades of dedicated service, strong community leadership, and enduring spirit left an indelible mark on our city.\line\line The City Council held a moment of silence in memory of Bob White.\b\i0\line\line\pard\b0\i At 6:50 PM, Mayor Lesser adjourned the meeting to the January 20, 2026, Adjourned Regular City Council Meeting at 5:00 PM.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


1.. Consideration of a Resolution Appointing Joseph DeFrancesco as Interim Public Works Director and Approval of an Employment Agreement with Joseph DeFrancesco (No Budget Impact) (Human Resources Director Jenkins).
(Estimated Time: 5 Mins.)
ADOPT RESOLUTION NO. 26-0003  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Amy Thomas Howorth {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian provided a brief statement on the item.\line\line Mayor Lesser announced that the resolution is to fulfill CalPERS requirements for the appointment of Joseph DeFranceso as Interim Public Works Director. As required by Government Code, it was reported that Mr. DeFranceso will be compensated at an hourly rate of $118.92 with no additional City benefits as a retiree.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments.\line\line\pard Seeing no requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\i0\f1\par
}


2.. Study Session Regarding Potential Development Impact Fees (Not Budgeted) (Finance Director Bretthauer).
(Estimated Time: 2 Hrs.)
DISCUSS AND PROVIDE DIRECTION {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Finance Director Libby Bretthauer provided the PowerPoint presentation.\line\line Harris & Associates Project Manager Adam Marston continued with the PowerPoint presentation and responded to City Council questions.\line\line Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson continued with the PowerPoint presentation on General Government Facilities and responded to City Council questions.\line\par
Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Police Fee and responded to City Council questions.\line\line Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Fire Protection Fee and responded to City Council questions.\line\line Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Transportation Fee Future Trip Generation and Wastewater Fee Buildout EDUs; and responded to City Council questions.\line\line Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Storm Drainage Fee Buildout EDUs and responded to City Council questions.\line\line Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Water Fee Buildout EDUs and Impact Fee Application Scenarios.\line\line City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian, Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson and City Engineer Gilbert Gamboa responded to City Council questions.\line\line Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Impact Fees in Other Cities and responded to City Council questions.\line\line Financial Services Manager Emy-Rose Hanna continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Anticipated Revenue and Funding Needed.\line\line Financial Services Manager Hanna and Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson responded to City Council questions.\line\line Financial Services Manager Emy-Rose Hanna continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Public Outreach & Required Notices.\line\par
Financial Services Manager Hanna and City Manager Mirzakhanian and responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Stefan Kampe\line Ray Joseph\line Trevor Boucher\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line\pard Finance Director Bretthauer, Harris & Associates Project Manager Martson and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\b The City Council directed staff to provide additional analysis with the Nexus Study, including real-life scenarios showing impacts on residents and surrounding cities, comparisons with neighboring cities, and clarification of key definitions beyond the Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs).\b0\i0\f1\par
}


